  "E18:conclusion": {
    "text": "Truncated BCH never reaches the Bayes floor on E1 (5.96/4.04/3.90 vs 2.79 deg) and at order 2 already costs >= the exact Hamilton product (~30 vs 28 scalar ops); the group law is the flop-cheapest EXACT composer. Quaternion-product multiplicative rank = 8 (de Groote), but Makarov's 8-mul algorithm needs 36 total ops > 28."
